.TH CAVA\-VIZ 1 "2025" "cava-viz 1.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
viz \- terminal audio visualizer using the CAVA FFT algorithm
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B viz
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B viz
is a real-time terminal audio visualizer built on the CAVA algorithm.
It captures audio from a PipeWire or PulseAudio monitor source, runs a
dual-channel FFT with Monstercat smoothing and autosensitivity, and renders
animated bar graphs in ncurses with truecolor gradients.
.PP
User-defined themes can be placed in
.I ~/.config/cava-viz/themes/
as
.I .theme
files. The configuration file is reloaded live whenever it changes on disk,
or on receipt of
.BR SIGHUP .
.SH OPTIONS
.SS General
.TP
.BI \-b " backend"
Audio backend to use.
.I backend
must be one of
.BR auto ,
.BR pipewire ,
or
.BR pulse .
Default:
.BR auto .
.TP
.BI \-s " source"
Explicit capture device name (as listed by
.BR --list-sources ).
Bypasses auto-detection entirely.
.TP
.B \-M
Capture from the default microphone instead of a monitor source.
.TP
.BI \-r " Hz"
PCM sample rate in Hz. Default:
.BR 44100 .
.TP
.BI \-t " index"
Starting theme index.
Built-in themes occupy indices 0\(en11; user themes follow in alphabetical
filename order starting at index 12.
.TP
.BI \-f " fps"
Target frame rate. Accepted range: 10\(en240. Default:
.BR 60 .
.TP
.B \-w
Automatically compute bar width to fill the terminal at startup.
.TP
.B \-\-list\-sources
Print all available PipeWire/PulseAudio sources and exit.
Indicates the default monitor and the last-used source.
.TP
.B \-\-check
Validate the configuration file, report user themes, and check audio source
availability. Exits with status 0 on success, 1 on failure.
.TP
.B \-V
Print the version string and exit.
.TP
.B \-h
Print a brief usage summary and exit.
.SS Bar mode (headless output)
Bar mode replaces the ncurses display with a stream of formatted bar strings
written to stdout, a FIFO, or a Unix socket. Designed for embedding in
status bars (Waybar, Polybar, lemonbar, eww, etc.).
.TP
.B \-\-bar
Enable bar mode. No ncurses is initialised.
.TP
.BI \-\-bar\-format " fmt"
Output format.
.I fmt
must be one of:
.RS
.TP
.B plain
Raw UTF-8 block characters, one line per frame. Works with eww, any shell script.
.TP
.B waybar
JSON with pango
.B <span color='#hex'>
markup. Use with Waybar's
.B "return-type": "json"
and
.BR "interval": "once" .
.TP
.B polybar
.B %{F#hex}...%{F-}
color tags. Also compatible with lemonbar.
.TP
.B eww
Identical to
.BR plain .
eww applies colours via CSS rather than inline tags.
.TP
.B raw
Space-separated floats in [0,\ 1], one per bar. Intended for custom consumers.
.TP
.B dzen2
.B ^fg(#hex)...^fg()
tags for dzen2.
.TP
.B i3bar
.B {"full_text":"...","color":"#hex"}
JSON block for i3bar.
.RE
.TP
.BI \-\-bar\-count " n"
Number of bars per channel. Default:
.BR 10 .
.TP
.BI \-\-bar\-chars " string"
UTF-8 string of level characters, ordered from lowest to highest.
Default:
.BR \[u2581]\[u2582]\[u2583]\[u2584]\[u2585]\[u2586]\[u2587]\[u2588] .
Any count \[>=]\ 2 is accepted; the levels are distributed evenly.
.TP
.BI \-\-bar\-color " #RRGGBB"
Accent color applied by tagged formats (waybar, polybar, dzen2, i3bar).
Default:
.BR #00ffcc .
.TP
.BI \-\-bar\-fps " n"
Output frame rate in bar mode. Lower values reduce CPU usage for status bars
that don't need 60\|fps. Default:
.BR 15 .
.TP
.BI \-\-bar\-stereo " mode"
Stereo handling.
.I mode
is either
.B merge
(average L+R into one bar string, default) or
.B split
(emit L\|<sep>\|R with separate channel strings).
.TP
.BI \-\-bar\-sep " string"
Separator used between channels in
.B split
stereo mode. Default:
.BR "\ |\ " .
.TP
.BI \-\-bar\-sink " type"
Output sink.
.I type
is one of
.B stdout
(default),
.B fifo
(named pipe), or
.B socket
(Unix domain socket server).
.TP
.BI \-\-bar\-out " path"
Filesystem path for the
.B fifo
or
.B socket
sink.
Required when
.B \-\-bar\-sink
is not
.BR stdout .
.SH KEYS
These keys are active in terminal (ncurses) mode only.
.TS
tab(|);
l l.
q|Quit
t|Cycle to next theme (built-in then user-defined)
g|Cycle gap width: 0 \[->] 1 \[->] 2 \[->] 0
] / [|Increase / decrease bar width
UP / DOWN|Adjust sensitivity manually
a|Toggle autosensitivity
s|Toggle stereo / mono
h|Toggle HUD pin (always visible vs auto-hide)
c|Toggle colour cycle (slow hue rotation)
v|Toggle per-bar colour (maps colour to bar position)
w|Toggle A-weighting (IEC 61672 perceptual curve)
n|Toggle auto-mono (collapse stereo when L \[~=] R)
.TE
.SH CONFIGURATION
The configuration file is created on first run at:
.PP
.RS
.I ${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-~/.config}/cava-viz/config
.RE
.PP
Edit it while the visualizer is running; changes are reloaded instantly via
inotify. Sending
.B SIGHUP
also triggers an immediate reload:
.PP
.RS
.B kill \-HUP $(pgrep viz)
.RE
.PP
Key-value format with
.B #
comments. All keys and their defaults:
.TS
tab(|);
l l l.
Key|Default|Description
_
theme|0|Theme index (0\(en11 built-in; 12+ user)
bar_width|2|Bar width in columns (1\(en8)
gap_width|1|Gap between bars (0\(en2)
hud_pinned|0|Always show HUD overlay
colour_cycle|0|Rotate gradient hue over time
per_bar_colour|0|Map colour to bar position
stereo|1|Stereo capture (0 = mono)
high_cutoff|10000|Upper frequency limit in Hz
gravity|1.00|Bar fall speed (0.1\(en5.0)
monstercat|1.50|Bar spread smoothing (0\(en5.0)
rise_factor|0.90|Attack smoothing (0\(en0.95)
bass_smooth|0.10|Extra bass smoothing (0\(en1.0)
a_weighting|0|IEC 61672 perceptual weighting
noise_gate|0.020|Bars below this snap to zero
auto_mono|0|Auto-collapse stereo when correlated
sensitivity|1.00|Manual sensitivity multiplier
auto_sens|1|Automatic sensitivity
fps|60|Target frame rate (10\(en240)
.TE
.SH USER THEMES
Place
.I .theme
files in:
.PP
.RS
.I ${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-~/.config}/cava-viz/themes/
.RE
.PP
Files are loaded in alphabetical filename order and cycle after the
twelve built-in themes. Adding, editing, or removing a
.I .theme
file reloads all user themes instantly without restarting.
.PP
Format:
.PP
.RS
.nf
# Optional comment
name   = My Theme

stop_0 = 0.00  #003366
stop_1 = 0.50  #0088cc
stop_2 = 1.00  #00ffcc
.fi
.RE
.PP
Rules:
.RS
.IP \[bu] 2
.I pos
runs from 0.0 (bar bottom) to 1.0 (bar top).
.IP \[bu]
Colors are
.I #RRGGBB
hex (upper or lowercase).
.IP \[bu]
2\(en8 stops required; stops may appear in any order.
.IP \[bu]
.B name
is optional and defaults to the filename without
.IR .theme .
.IP \[bu]
Lines starting with
.B #
are comments.
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-~/.config}/cava-viz/config
Main configuration file.
.TP
.I ${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-~/.config}/cava-viz/state
Persists the last-used audio source across restarts.
.TP
.I ${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-~/.config}/cava-viz/themes/
Directory for user-defined
.I .theme
files.
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGINT, SIGTERM
Quit cleanly, restoring the terminal.
.TP
.B SIGHUP
Reload the configuration file and user themes immediately.
.TP
.B SIGWINCH
Redraw at the new terminal size.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Auto-detect backend and monitor source:
.B viz
.TP
Force PipeWire with a specific source:
.B viz \-b pipewire \-s alsa_output.pci-0000_00_1f.3.monitor
.TP
Microphone visualizer, Aurora theme, 30\|fps:
.B viz \-M \-t 6 \-f 30
.TP
Waybar integration (add to Waybar config):
.nf
"custom/viz": {
    "exec": "viz --bar --bar-format waybar --bar-count 12",
    "return-type": "json",
    "interval": "once",
    "restart-interval": 5
}
.fi
.TP
FIFO for tmux status bar:
.nf
viz --bar --bar-sink fifo --bar-out /tmp/viz.pipe &
# In tmux.conf:
set \-g status\-right "#(cat /tmp/viz.pipe)"
.fi
.TP
List available audio sources:
.B viz \-\-list\-sources
.TP
Validate configuration:
.B viz \-\-check
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pactl (1),
.BR pipewire (1),
.BR pulseaudio (1),
.BR waybar (5)
